\ Strict-mode positive case: a swap that reorders an opaque row now compiles. A
\ runtime-depth `drop-at` collapses the stack into a row; pushing a literal above
\ it and swapping it under the row top is emitted as a native swap against the
\ live physical stack and collapses to a fresh row pinned at slot 0 beneath the
\ swapped pair, rather than rejecting as an abstract underflow. Under
\ --interpreter-fallback=false the build
\ must succeed and run correctly. This is the discriminate-then-shuffle shape of
\ `(lexer-step)`'s false arm, isolated to the offending swap.
10 20 30 40 50 0 drop-at 99 swap . . . . .
